4. The Marginal Gain for Humanity

The concept of marginal gains proposes that many small improvements can combine into a substantial overall advantage.

We propose a related concept: Marginal Gains for All Humanity.

The procedure is straightforward.

First, identify something you personally consider beneficial.

Next, increase it slightly.

Then increase it again.

Continue until the benefit becomes sufficiently large that consulting other people appears unnecessary.

For example:

This software helps people write emails.

becomes

This software improves productivity.

which becomes

This software increases economic output.

which becomes

This software raises global living standards.

which becomes

This software benefits humanity.

At no point is humanity required to interrupt the derivation.

This is mathematically convenient.

