7. The Humanity Spokesperson Paradox

We define the Humanity Spokesperson Paradox:

The probability that somebody publicly claims to speak for humanity increases approximately in proportion to the probability that humanity has never heard of them.

This creates unusual situations.

A founder may announce:

“Humanity must prepare for the transition.”

Several billion members of humanity may respond:

“The transition to what?”

The resulting disagreement is frequently classified as a communications challenge.

The possibility that humanity understood the proposal perfectly well and simply possesses different priorities receives comparatively little attention.

