10. Proposed Governance Improvement: Ask Humanity Occasionally

We propose a radical governance mechanism.

Ask people.

Not merely investors.

Not merely experts.

Not merely employees.

Not merely people already convinced by the premise.

People.

This will undoubtedly introduce inefficiency.

People will disagree.

Some will misunderstand things.

Some will demand impossible compromises.

Some will have terrible ideas.

Some may even vote for things experts consider objectively stupid.

Unfortunately, this is one of the irritating properties of sharing civilisation with other humans.

They possess agency.

A future genuinely belonging to humanity must therefore contain at least some humanity in the decision-making process.

